        ("Volatility", "Diffusion: standard deviation of the 20 daily log returns up to 2 October. With the jump: root mean square of the last 20 returns, including 5 October. Jump-robust: bipower variation, π/2 times the mean product of adjacent absolute returns. Long run: standard deviation since 2003."),
        ("Random-walk benchmark", "Zero drift; daily volatility for {sessions_to_runoff} − 1 sessions plus one session with the root-mean-square move of the first PTAX after the six completed runoffs ({runoff_rms}). The share of paths below a level is the normal cumulative distribution of the log distance divided by the horizon’s standard deviation. A benchmark for the rule, not a forecast."),
        ("Commodity basket", "Brent, soybeans, iron ore, coffee, sugar and maize (IMF monthly benchmarks via FRED), weighted by their share of Brazil’s 2025 goods exports (UN Comtrade, HS 2709, 1201, 2601, 0901, 1701, 1005) and re-scaled to sum to 100%. Monthly USD/BRL is the average of daily PTAX."),
